{"type":"standard","title":"Ryan Fazio","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ryan Fazio</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q108130263","titles":{"canonical":"Ryan_Fazio","normalized":"Ryan Fazio","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ryan Fazio</span></span>"},"pageid":68501908,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Ryan_Fazio%2C_2026_%283x4_headshot%29.jpg/330px-Ryan_Fazio%2C_2026_%283x4_headshot%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e4/Ryan_Fazio%2C_2026_%283x4_headshot%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3502,"height":4672},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376093719","tid":"33d6f85e-b624-11f1-91c9-8a964350d8ce","timestamp":"2026-09-22T01:23:23Z","description":"State Senator from Connecticut","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Fazio","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Fazio?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Fazio?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ryan_Fazio"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Fazio","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ryan_Fazio","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Fazio?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ryan_Fazio"}},"extract":"Ryan Michael Fazio is an American businessman and politician who is a member of the Connecticut State Senate for the 36th district. A member of the Republican Party, he won election in 2021 following the resignation of Democratic incumbent Alexandra Kasser, and was re-elected in 2022 and 2024.","extract_html":"<p><b>Ryan Michael Fazio</b> is an American businessman and politician who is a member of the Connecticut State Senate for the 36th district. A member of the Republican Party, he won election in 2021 following the resignation of Democratic incumbent Alexandra Kasser, and was re-elected in 2022 and 2024.</p>"}